--- body ---
## Context
After tickets 0116 (schema-literal struct) and 0117 (validating-parser
merge), two `Erg` fields still carry raw strings that the parser already
has enough information to type:

- `BlockedBys []string` — each entry is a `Blocked-by:` value that the
  ref grammar can already parse. Lazy parsing via `BlockedByRefs()` is
  the last surviving accessor method after 0116.
- `Created string` — a date the validator regex-checks. Parsing to
  `time.Time` at parse time turns malformed dates into structured
  parse errors and gives downstream code a real value.

This ticket completes the type alignment.

## Proposed changes
1. `BlockedBys []string` → `BlockedBys []Ref`. Each ref is parsed at
   parse time; malformed values become `ParseError`s from 0117's pass.
   Delete `BlockedByRefs()`.
2. `Created string` → `Created time.Time`. ISO date parsed at parse
   time; malformed value becomes a `ParseError`.
3. Update all call sites that read these fields (today's accessors are
   already gone after 0116; call sites just read the typed fields).
4. Output paths (JSON serialization, log lines) format the typed values
   back to strings where needed — single conversion point.

## Out of scope
- Other field types (`Title`, `Author`, `Closed`, `Tags`) remain
  strings; they have no richer type to graduate to.

## Dependencies
- Hard dep: ticket 0117 (validating-parser merge). The parse-time
  error channel introduced there is where malformed refs and dates
  flow as parse errors.

## Exit criteria
- `Erg.BlockedBys` is `[]Ref`; `Erg.Created` is `time.Time`.
- No accessor methods remain on `Erg` for these fields.
- Malformed refs / dates produce parse errors via 0117's mechanism.
- `make test` passes; output paths format `time.Time` back to the
  spec's `YYYY-MM-DD` form.
